{"units": [{"id": "pythochrestes-word1", "translation": "Orestes, the one ordained by Pytho"}, {"id": "pythochrestes-word2", "translation": "ordained by Pytho"}, {"id": "pythochrestes-word3", "translation": "the young man ordained by Loxias's Pythian oracle"}, {"id": "pythochrestes-word4", "translation": "the Pythian-ordained leader of the colony"}, {"id": "pythochrestos-orth1", "translation": "ordained by the Pythian oracle"}, {"id": "pythochrestos-def1", "translation": "ordained by the Pythian oracle"}, {"id": "pythochrestos-quote1", "translation": "the Pythian-ordained prophecies"}, {"id": "pytho-orth1", "translation": "Pytho"}, {"id": "pytho-def1", "translation": "Pytho, a city of Phocis, commonly called Delphi"}, {"id": "pytho-quote1", "translation": "he sent frequent envoys to Pytho and to Dodona"}, {"id": "pykaes-orth1", "translation": "pointed, sharp"}, {"id": "pykaes-def1", "translation": "See πευκήεις."}, {"id": "pykaes-word1", "translation": "pointed, sharp"}, {"id": "pyknos-orth1", "translation": "dense, frequent"}, {"id": "pyknos-def1", "translation": "dense, frequent"}, {"id": "pyknos-quote1", "translation": "he sent frequent envoys"}, {"id": "pyknos-quote2", "translation": "looking with close-set eyes"}, {"id": "pyknos-quote3", "translation": "receiving a dense beating"}, {"id": "pyknos-quote4", "translation": "entwined with dense serpents"}, {"id": "pyknos-quote5", "translation": "of the frequent kisses"}, {"id": "pyknoma-orth1", "translation": "a close-woven fabric"}, {"id": "pyknoma-def1", "translation": "a close-woven fabric"}, {"id": "pyknoma-note1", "translation": "Concerning garments woven with the spatha, on account of the density they thereby acquired. Hesychius σπάθημα: πύκνωμα, ἀπὸ τῶν ταῖς σπάθαις κατακρουόντων τὰ ὕφη [spathema: pyknoma, from those who beat the web with the spathae]: from which it can be inferred that πυκνώμασι [with close-woven fabrics] was introduced from a gloss in place of σπαθήμασι [with spathae-woven fabrics], as conjectured by Wecklein, Stud. Aesch. p. 34, and Herwerden in Stud. crit. p. 1."}, {"id": "pyknoma-quote1", "translation": "luxuriating in barbarian robes and close-woven fabrics"}, {"id": "pyknoma-word1", "translation": "spathema: pyknoma, from those who beat the web with the spathae"}, {"id": "pyknoma-word2", "translation": "with close-woven fabrics"}, {"id": "pyknoma-word3", "translation": "with spathae-woven fabrics"}, {"id": "pylades-orth1", "translation": "Pylades"}, {"id": "pylades-def1", "translation": "Pylades, son of Strophius and Anaxibia, companion of Orestes, who comes on stage in the Choephori"}, {"id": "pylades-quote1", "translation": "Pylades"}, {"id": "pylades-quote2", "translation": "Pylades"}, {"id": "pyle-orth1", "translation": "gate"}, {"id": "pyle-def1", "translation": "gate. Aeschylus used only the plural number."}, {"id": "pyle-note1", "translation": "where by a later hand is written above πυλῶν πυργώματα [the towers of the gates]"}, {"id": "pyle-note2", "translation": "μοχλοῖς χαλᾶτε [loosen with the bars]. Where he calls the women's gates the gate leading to the women's quarters: about which Blomfield spoke in his annotation."}, {"id": "pyle-quote1", "translation": "at the narrow gates of the lake"}, {"id": "pyle-quote2", "translation": "the gates of the towers"}, {"id": "pyle-quote3", "translation": "at the exits of the gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote4", "translation": "to the gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote5", "translation": "they stand at the [seventh] gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote6", "translation": "a din at the gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote7", "translation": "a roar at the gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote8", "translation": "and a crashing at the gates is increased"}, {"id": "pyle-quote9", "translation": "as each at the gates has obtained his lot"}, {"id": "pyle-quote10", "translation": "at the Proetid gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote11", "translation": "of the gates of Proetus"}, {"id": "pyle-quote12", "translation": "he has obtained the Electran gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote13", "translation": "having obtained other gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote14", "translation": "the one who obtained from there the post at the gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote15", "translation": "at the Neistan gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote16", "translation": "to have fallen at the gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote17", "translation": "he will go out from the gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote18", "translation": "having neighboring gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote19", "translation": "he boasts at the gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote20", "translation": "a neighbor to the gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote21", "translation": "before the gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote22", "translation": "stationed at the fifth, the Borraean gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote23", "translation": "he stands at the gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote24", "translation": "within the gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote25", "translation": "stationed at the Homoloid gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote26", "translation": "to attack the gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote27", "translation": "at the seventh gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote28", "translation": "we have fenced ourselves at the gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote29", "translation": "at the gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote30", "translation": "he has gone swiftly through the gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote31", "translation": "to open the gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote32", "translation": "the gates of Hades"}, {"id": "pyle-quote33", "translation": "to the courtyard gates"}, {"id": "pyle-quote34", "translation": "why do you keep the suppliant from the gates?"}, {"id": "pyle-quote35", "translation": "having thrown the courtyard gate"}, {"id": "pyle-quote36", "translation": "the gates of the house"}, {"id": "pyle-quote37", "translation": "the women's gates"}, {"id": "pyle-word1", "translation": "the towers of the gates"}, {"id": "pyle-word2", "translation": "loosen with the bars"}, {"id": "pyle-word3", "translation": "the women's gates"}, {"id": "pyle-word4", "translation": "the women's quarters"}, {"id": "pyloma-orth1", "translation": "gate"}, {"id": "pyloma-def1", "translation": "gate"}, {"id": "pyloma-quote1", "translation": "the guardian of the gates"}, {"id": "pyloma-quote2", "translation": "in six gates"}, {"id": "pyloros-orth1", "translation": "gatekeeper"}, {"id": "pyloros-def1", "translation": "gatekeeper, doorkeeper, janitor"}, {"id": "pyloros-quote1", "translation": "we will set against him a gatekeeper hostile to strangers"}, {"id": "punthanomai-orth1", "translation": "to learn, inquire"}]}